{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful figure in the 12th century Mediterranean world a ruler known for his military prowess and political acumen. He served as Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1193 leaving a legacy of expansion and consolidation of power. His reign marked a significant period of stability and prosperity for the Countship.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension* Raymond was born in 1128 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and his wife Adela of Blois. He received a comprehensive education in warfare diplomacy and administration preparing him for his future role. After his father's death in 1152 Raymond ascended to the countship inheriting a territory that encompassed coastal regions of present-day Lebanon Syria and Palestine. His early years were marked by consolidating his authority and dealing with internal rebellions and external threats. He skillfully navigated the complex political landscape of the Crusader states and the Byzantine Empire.\n\nRaymond III’s reign witnessed significant territorial gains. He expanded the Countship’s influence through military campaigns and strategic alliances. He successfully defended Tripoli against Muslim incursions and extended his control over neighboring regions.  He fostered trade and economic growth establishing important commercial relationships with Venice Genoa and other maritime powers. His administration was known for its efficiency and its commitment to justice and the rule of law.  He implemented reforms in taxation infrastructure and legal systems benefiting the local population.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts* Raymond III was a renowned military leader who engaged in numerous campaigns throughout his reign. He actively defended Tripoli’s borders against various Muslim dynasties including the Ayyubids and the Mamluks. He also participated in Crusades fighting alongside the Christian kingdoms of Europe.  His military campaigns were characterized by tactical brilliance and effective leadership. He secured key territories and fortifications strengthening Tripoli’s defenses.  He also engaged in conflicts with other Crusader states vying for control of the Levant.\n\nRaymond III’s legacy extends beyond his military achievements. He is remembered as a wise and just ruler who fostered economic growth and social stability. He patronized the arts and sciences and promoted cultural exchange. He established a strong and independent government that served as a model for other Crusader states. He is considered a pivotal figure in the history of the Levant and a symbol of the Crusader presence in the Eastern Mediterranean. He died in 1193 leaving behind a prosperous and secure Countship that continued to thrive for several decades.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.14342188835144043}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.5060096454108134e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0798519179224968}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04111293703317642}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5501455068588257}, {"token": "▁figure", "logprob": -1.6038830280303955}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.024912608787417412}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.003749603871256113}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.6708590984344482}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.0015584002248942852}, {"token": "th", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁century", "logprob": -0.04174918308854103}, {"token": "▁Mediterranean", "logprob": -1.1756385564804077}, {"token": "▁world", "logprob": -0.0005523824947886169}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -1.3093938827514648}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5215843915939331}, {"token": "▁known", "logprob": -1.090301752090454}, {"token": "▁for", "logprob": -0.002198661444